{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775392291-irsJeadYggiPAg6e1bEb","role":"assistant","created":1775392310,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, I need to reconsider the question. The question asks about \"total balance values\" from \"official trust account statements on social security programs\". \n\nLooking at the table, the \"Balance\" section has:\n- Total investments\n- Unexpended balance (which has two sub-columns: In General Fund and In disbursing officer's account)\n\nThe \"Total\" column in the Balance section seems to actually represent \"Total investments\" based on the table structure. Let me re-read the table more carefully.\n\nActually wait - looking at the table more carefully:\n\nThe Balance section has three columns: \"Total\", \"Investments\", and \"Unexpended balance\". But wait, in the HTML the columns are:\n- Total\n- Investments  \n- Unexpended balance (with subcolumns: In General Fund, In disbursing officer's account)\n\nActually for Table 3, it shows:\n- Total investments\n- Unexpended balance\n\nSo the balance is really Total investments + Unexpended balance. But wait, that doesn't seem right either. Let me look more carefully at the table headers:\n\nFor Table 3 (Unemployment Trust Fund):\n- Balance section has: Total investments | Unexpended balance\n\nSo the \"Total\" column is actually \"Total investments\" and there's also \"Unexpended balance\" separately.\n\nActually, looking at the table again:\nThe Balance section in the table shows: Total investments | Unexpended balance\n\nBut wait - for the other tables, the Balance section shows: Total | Investments | Unexpended balance (with subcolumns)\n\nLet me re-examine. Looking at Table 1 for Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance Trust Fund:\n- Balance: Total | Investments | Unexpended balance (with subcolumns: In General Fund, In disbursing officer's account)\n\nSo for Table 1, \"Total\" is the total balance.\n\nFor Table 3 (Unemployment Trust Fund), looking at the header:\n`<th colspan=\"3\">Balance</th>`\n\n\n- Total investments\n- Unexpended balance\n\nI'm seeing a discrepancy between the table structure and the actual data. The \"Total\" column in the balance section appears to represent the total balance, not just investments. The numbers in this column are what I'll use to calculate the 4-year moving averages for the Unemployment Trust Fund.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_ee87c09f66c04a2287693e27","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Looking at the table more carefully, the Balance section's 'Total' column \n# represents the total balance (which is Total investments + Unexpended balance)\n# Let's verify by looking at 1936: 18.9 (total) vs investments 18.9 + unexpended *\n\n# Actually looking at Table 1 as reference, the 'Total' is the main balance column\n# For Table 3 the Balance shows: Total investments | Unexpended balance\n# But wait, looking at the numbers - Total investments matches the 'Total' for most rows\n# Let me check the columns more carefully\n\n# Looking at the data again:\n# 1936: Total = 18.9 (matches Total investments = 18.9)\n# 1937: Total = 312.4 (matches Total investments = 312.3 + 0.1 unexpended)\n# 1938: Total = 884.2 (matches Total investments = 872.0 + 12.2 unexpended)\n# etc.\n\n# The question asks for 'total balance values' - this would be Total investments + Unexpended\n# Let me recalculate properly\n\nbalances = {\n    1936: 18.9,     # 18.9 + * (essentially 18.9)\n    1937: 312.4,    # 312.3 + 0.1\n    1938: 884.2,    # 872.0 + 12.2\n    1939: 1270.5,   # 1257.0 + 13.5\n    1940: 1723.4,   # 1710.0 + 13.4\n    1941: 2281.0,   # 2273.0 + 8.0\n    1942: 3146.8    # 3139.0 + 7.8\n}\n\n# Wait, I should double check: for 1942 the balance is 3146.8 or is the 'Total' column really showing Total investments only?\n# Looking at the table: Balance shows Total investments | Unexpended balance\n# The numbers under 'Total investments' column and the values in the balance row match differently\n\n# Actually I think I've been misreading. Let me look at the raw data again:\n# For 1936: there's only one value 18.9 in the balance row - that's Total\n# For 1937: 312.4 - that's the Total\n# The table shows 'Total investments' and separately 'Unexpended balance'\n# So Total = investments + unexpended\n\n# Let me use the exact values from the 'Total' (which represents total balance)\n# Looking at the data, I'll use these values:\n\nbalances = {\n    1936: 18.9,\n    1937: 312.4,\n    1938: 884.2,\n    1939: 1270.5,\n    1940: 1723.4,\n    1941: 2281.0,\n    1942: 3146.8\n}\n\n# 4-year moving averages\nma_1936_1939 = (balances[1936] + balances[1937] + balances[1938] + balances[1939]) / 4\nma_1937_1940 = (balances[1937] + balances[1938] + balances[1939] + balances[1940]) / 4\nma_1938_1941 = (balances[1938] + balances[1939] + balances[1940] + balances[1941]) / 4\nma_1939_1942 = (balances[1939] + balances[1940] + balances[1941] + balances[1942]) / 4\n\nprint(f'1936-1939: {ma_1936_1939:.1f}')\nprint(f'1937-1940: {ma_1937_1940:.1f}')\nprint(f'1938-1941: {ma_1938_1941:.1f}')\nprint(f'1939-1942: {ma_1939_1942:.1f}')\n\nmoving_averages = [ma_1936_1939, ma_1937_1940, ma_1938_1941, ma_1939_1942]\nprint(f'\\\\nRange: {min(moving_averages):.1f} - {max(moving_averages):.1f}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
